<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Oct manufacturing output up 2.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch Oct manufacturing output up 2.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch seasonally adjusted manufacturing production fell 0.2 percent in October compared with September, the Central Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>But October manufacturing production was 2.9 percent higher than in the same month of 1995, the CBS added.  </p>
<p>    DUTCH MANUFACTURING PRODUCTION    Oct 96    Sep 96    Oct 95</p>
<p>seasonally adjusted</p>
<p>    index (base 1990)			107.9     108.2     105.0</p>
<p>    month-on-month pct change	     -0.2	-0.4	-0.7</p>
<p>non-seasonally adjusted</p>
<p>    index (base 1990)			112.9     110.5     109.8</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change		 +2.9	+2.4	-0.8</p>
<p>NOTE - CBS calculates month-on-month changes on basis of seasonally adjusted index and year-on-year changes on basis of non-seasonally adjusted index.  </p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
